The pages and tarballs associated with the linux scsi
generic driver and related utilities have been moved from
www.torque.net/sg (also known as sg.torque.net/sg) to
   http://sg.danny.cz/sg

Some of the packages and individual utilities found at this site
are:
   - sg3_utils
   - smp_utils
   - sdparm
   - lsscsi

The links on the http://freshmeat.net site for sg3_utils and
sdparm have been updated.


The torque.net domain has been the home of the scsi generic
driver for around 10 years. It was run by Grant Guenther who
is the author of the parallel generic (pg) driver in linux.
It was shutdown about a month ago and the domain name sold.
The new owner is forwarding email (dougg@torque.net) but
dgilbert@interlog.com will be more reliable from now on.

I would like to thank Dan Horak (dan@danny.cz) for adopting
my orphaned sg website.

